---
/**
 * FIG. 04: what the page does not claim, in the words of the Clear Signing
 * page's "What we don't claim". "Attested" appears only as the schema allows
 * it: for a descriptor whose ERC-8176 attestation verified.
 */
import Section from "../home/Section.astro";
import { attested, count, days, described, registryUrl, report, sampleSize } from "./report.ts";

interface Props {
  id: string;
}

const { id } = Astro.props;
const { registry, sources } = report;
---

<Section {id} fig="FIG. 04" eyebrow="Limits" title="What this page does not claim">
  <ul class="claims rise">
    <li>
      <strong>Being in the registry is not an audit.</strong> The registry's maintainers screen submissions, and inclusion
      is not an endorsement. A descriptor says what a call does, not whether the contract is safe to call.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A descriptor is not attested unless its attestation verifies.</strong> An attestation is a reviewer's signed
      claim about one exact descriptor, under ERC-8176, which is still a draft. We call a descriptor attested only when its
      attestation verified and has not been revoked: {count(attested.length)} of the {count(described.length)} contracts
      here with a descriptor.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our drafts are drafts.</strong> A B3Pay draft is a descriptor we wrote and tested on real transactions. It is
      not in the registry, so no wallet reads it yet, and its preview shows how one call would read, not how any wallet
      shows it today.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A sample is not all traffic.</strong> The shares come from up to {count(sampleSize)} recent transactions for
      each contract, read {days(sources.onchain.oldest, sources.onchain.newest)}. They describe those transactions, and
      they move as traffic does.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Wallets decide.</strong> Each wallet chooses which registries and which reviewers it trusts. That a wallet
      could clear-sign a call means the registry holds what it needs, not that every wallet shows it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="sourced rise">
    Sources: <a href={registryUrl}>the Clear Signing registry</a> at <code>{registry.commit.slice(0, 7)}</code>,{" "}
    <a href="https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8176">ERC-8176</a>, <a href="https://www.blockscout.com/">Blockscout</a>{" "}
    and <a href="https://sourcify.dev/">Sourcify</a>. How a descriptor works is in{" "}
    <a href="/docs/clear-signing/">the docs</a>.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .claims {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .claims li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  /* A short amber dash, the site's list mark on a quiet page. */
  .claims li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.85rem;
    left: 0;
    width: 0.75rem;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--brand);
  }

  .claims strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sourced {
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .sourced a {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
  }

  .sourced code {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: inherit;
  }
</style>
